# npm packs the working tree, not the git index. On a clone with
# core.autocrlf=true that would ship bin/vno.js with a CRLF shebang, and every
# Linux/macOS install would die with `env: 'node\r': No such file or directory`.
# Forcing LF in the working tree is what keeps the published binary runnable.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
